{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Not distressed.</b> The truth is that it is with a vav, like the sense of ותקצר נפשו (Judges 10:16) — by way of analogy, to make [the hearers] understand, as though He too were in distress, therefore He hastened to save them:" "<b>And the angel of His presence saved them.</b> And thus it is written, וישלח מלאך ויוציאנו ממצרים (Numbers 20:16) [and He sent an angel and brought us out of Egypt], and it is not Moses at all:" "<b>And He bore them.</b> Like ונטל החול (Proverbs 27:3) [and the bearing of sand]. Now the sense is that He redeemed them from Egypt and bore them in their land; therefore He said, כל ימי עולם [all the days of eternity] — all the days that they were in their land:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 63, :notes {0 "The bracketed [השומעים] appears in the source; bracketed text is Ibn Ezra's own insertion.", 1 "The source cites Numbers 21:19 but the verse quoted matches Numbers 20:16; translated as printed."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:49.674448350Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}